("DR-265","Monitoring: score and feature PSI against the manifest reference bins, override rate from phase 18 decision types against the top band; green, amber, red bands with governed thresholds (`psi_watch` max 0.10, `psi_action` max 0.25, `override_rate_action` max 0.30); a red point opens one phase 24 register finding (source `model_monitor`) closed with RETRAINED, RECALIBRATED, RESTRICTED_USE, RULES_ONLY or JUSTIFIED_NO_ACTION; jobs count every tier and reads show only suppressed window aggregates","Research 29 9d, GV-18, GV-19, GV-21 (lead review: all tiers counted, as phase 24 `str_rate`)"),
("DR-266","Model kill switch (global or per family) engages at once under step-up `approval` by an MRO with no change request; release is a change request on `cr_material` (MLRO and CHK); each family's `model_kill_state` row is created with the family; drills quarterly drive a phase 24 calendar row","GV-20, MAS 6.5.6; same safe-direction rule as DR-108"),
("DR-267","A pinned family refuses promotion of another version until unpinned; a phase 25 release imports model artifacts as `registered` only; a starter family's first live goes through the same promotion change request; only one family is live per install (second family refused `other_family_live`)","GV-29; a release never replaces a version the bank approved"),
("DR-268","Model features are checked against the phase 24 protected-attribute register at import (prohibited inputs, allowed-use matrix with use `score`, proxy rule, screening sources never a normal-tier feature); the sensitivity sweep proves geography, residence and nationality are never a sole trigger; model fairness is phase 24 metric `score_top_band_rate`","GV-36, GV-37, GV-38; the matrix is data, not code"),
("DR-269","Reason codes are the three largest positive contributions of an in-house interventional TreeSHAP on the stored trees, checked against golden rows; they are catalogue feature keys with Arabic and English labels from phase 13 `name`; only three are shown","GV-41, TS-16, phase 17 UX-08"),
("DR-270","Scores and reason codes are read through the phase 17 visibility predicate and phase 03 suspicion masking with the alert's own purpose rules; shadow and challenger scores are never returned; monitoring, ladder and override reads are suppressed window counts; no export or notice carries a score","Phase 17 rules 1 and 2, GV-40, tipping-off"),
